# Sample GRIB File

This is a placeholder for a sample GRIB file.

## Description

A sample GRIB file containing meteorological data for testing and demonstration purposes with cfgrib.

## Typical Contents

- Surface fields: 2m temperature, 10m wind components, surface pressure
- Pressure level fields: Temperature, geopotential, wind components
- Multiple time steps: Analysis and forecast steps
- Grid: Regular latitude-longitude grid

## File Size

Typical size: 1-10 MB depending on resolution and number of fields

## How to Obtain

Sample GRIB files can be obtained from:
- ECMWF Public Dataset: https://www.ecmwf.int/en/forecasts/datasets
- NCEP GFS: https://www.nco.ncep.noaa.gov/pmb/data/gfs/
- NOAA NOMADS: https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/

## Example Usage

```python
import xarray as xr

# Read GRIB file
ds = xr.open_dataset('sample_grib.grib', engine='cfgrib')

# Inspect dataset
print(ds)
print(ds.data_vars)
print(ds.coords)

# Access data
temperature = ds['t2m']
print(f"Temperature shape: {temperature.shape}")
print(f"Temperature mean: {temperature.mean():.2f} K")

# Close dataset
ds.close()
```

## Notes

- This is a text placeholder file
- Actual GRIB files are binary and cannot be represented as text
- Replace this file with an actual GRIB file for testing